  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "On our testing server, out of a batch of thousands of fixity service calls we saw hundreds of BAD_CHECKSUM responses.  In spot-checking the objects, further calls to the fixity service always produced a SUCCESS response.  The logging in this area of the code is not verbose and Fedora does not raise an exception or log a warning or error when a BAD_CHECKSUM is returned (from ModeShape I guess).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I suspect this problem may prove difficult or impossible to reproduce, but I wanted to record it officially.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
